---
import { LayerCard } from "@cloudflare/kumo/components/layer-card";
import C from "../components/C.astro";
import P from "../components/P.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import { figure } from "../lib/styles";

const pill =
  "flex h-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-kumo-base px-4 font-mono text-lg leading-none font-medium whitespace-nowrap text-kumo-strong shadow-xs ring ring-kumo-line select-none";
const op =
  "flex size-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-kumo-base font-mono text-lg leading-none text-kumo-subtle shadow-xs ring ring-kumo-line select-none";
const beats = ["glide", "settle", "press", "release"];
---

<Section id="how" title="How it works">
  <P>
    Every step is a small piece of hand motion. A click isn't a jump cut: the cursor travels there in a
    slight arc, rests for a beat so your eye catches up, presses, and lets go.
  </P>
  <figure class={figure}>
    <LayerCard className="w-full bg-kumo-elevated">
      <p class="flex w-full flex-col items-center justify-center gap-4 py-16 sm:flex-row sm:gap-2">
        {
          beats.map((b, i) => (
            <>
              {i > 0 && <span class={op}>→</span>}
              <span class={pill}>{b}</span>
            </>
          ))
        }
      </p>
    </LayerCard>
  </figure>
  <P>
    The press fires real <C>pointerdown</C>, <C>mousedown</C>, <C>pointerup</C>, <C>mouseup</C> and <C>click</C> events
    on the element, so your app's own handlers run. Typing writes through the native value setter and fires{" "}
    <C>input</C>, so React and Vue controlled fields update too.
  </P>
  <P>
    The camera is a transform on the stage's only child. The cursor lives inside it, so it scales with the zoom and stays
    on its target while the camera moves.
  </P>
</Section>
